Ascension of a Monk

I am executing alphabetically ordered series of ascension, which
started with Archeologist in December 2009 (also my very first NetHack
ascension). Over the next year I ascended Barbarian, Caveman, Healer
and Knight. And the series was extended by my Monk ascension today.

I had several rather advanced Monk games before. One ended with being
killed by Master Kaen, other ended post-quest at Castle from a monster
summoned by some angel there (I was playing too carelessly).

My neutral human male Monk started with scroll of identify and he used
it on the first spellbook he found - which turned out to be a
spellbook of identify.

Some time later on dlvl 5 he found bones of wizard called tmrykr
containing another spellbook of identify, magic marker with 0:96
charges, cloak of magic resistance and, quite importantly for a monk,
+5 ring of increase damage. Quite a lucky find.

He did Sokoban first, netting him a brand new bag of holding.

Mines were not very interesting (altar crossaligned, nothing very
useful in Minetown shops).

After some time my Monk had two uncursed ruby rings, so he dropped one
into a sink and found out, that it is ring of teleport control.

At dlvl 17 throne room was found. This throne room gave Mr. Monk two
wishes in a row and as a bonus level mapping. He wished for amulet of
reflection and Orb of Fate. Normally I don't artiwish, but since Monk
can really use Orb's half damage effect, I broke my own rules here.

Sacrificing and praying (Mr. Monk had quite a selection, two coaligned
temple and two more altars) yielded some spellbooks and intrinsic
telepathy.

Found cursed scroll of genocide found its use at the top of Sokoban,
where my Monk held a dance party with some nice nurses, gaining better
health in process.

The stumbling block of Monk mid-game is of course Master Kaen. In my
previous kill I polymorphed my Monk into a black dragon and
disintegrated Kaen. It worked, but it was very close call as Mr. Monk
got mere 20 hitpoints from death. At any rate, my monk did not have
ring of polymorph control nor amulet of unchanging, so I had to devise
another plan for him. He arrived at Kaen's lair, created boulder fort
with scroll of earth, burned Elbereth into stairs and waited for
Master Kaen to arrive. And waited and waited, and Kaen was meditating
and showed no intention of coming to meet his challenger. Given no
other option, monk had to teleport out of his fort, wake Kaen and
teleport back. Then he killed him by throwing shurikens and darts at
him.

Medusa and Castle were nominal, except some difficulties at Castle
with a ki-rin that kept summoning monsters. The difficult situation
was made manageable by Orb of Fate's half damage. Wand of wishing had
one initial charge, that was used for charging scrolls, one charge
from recharged wand was used to wish for helm of brilliance.

Then our hero established his main stash at VoTD, while also reaching
XL 17, which for monks means intrinsic teleport control. Donating to
the priest of Moloch netted another point of protection, so naked AC
was now -2.

Mapping Gehennom was the usual chore, but he had stack of scrolls of
magic mapping and the Eyes helped, too, so it was rather swift
process. Especially as spellbook of magic mapping was found at Vlad's
Tower. Monk slew or bribed all the demon princes except Orcus.

Lower Fake Wizard's Tower was infested with gremlins, so monk started
to slay them with his martial arts. Suddenly "Gremlin chuckles. You
feel paranoid." message appears as one of the gremlins stole Monk's
invisibility intrinsic. I thought MC3 protects against the intrinsic
stealing attack, but I was wrong. Fortunately, invisibility is easily
restored.

Dlvl 49 was VS level, but it was pain to find the vibrating square
itself. After it was found, monk levelported to VoTD and packed for
ascension run. He also used last three wishes from his wand of wishing
to wish for ring of free action, ring of conflict and two scrolls of
gold detection (as these were never found in dungeon). The final wish
from only magic lamp was left available for emergencies.

Then monk scoured Gehennom until he found cockatrice, that was willing
to leave corpse when slain. With c corpse he levelported below Orcus
Town, went upstairs and in one fell turn stoned Orcus and retrieved
his 0:5 wand of death (so the monk now had 2 wands of death).

Slaying Wizard of Yendor was fine, but again, there was gremlin plague
that needed to be dealt with. After invocation, Mr. Monk levelported
to Moloch's Sanctum ending right in front of secret doors.
Unfortunately, just as he was fighting the high priest of Moloch,
Rodney appeared and started to make serious mischief. First he stole
the Eyes of Overworld (getting magic resistant), then cast Double
Trouble. Monk expended three charges from wand of death before he
realized that he has to fight the wizard in mele=E9 and that was far
from easy. Also, he was wearing robe and needed to switch to cloak of
magic resistance, leaving him prone for several turns. Monk killed the
high priest first, so Rodney took the amulet and teleported to
upstairs. To avoid the gruelling travel through all the Moloch's
Sanctum, monk levelported up and came down via stairs.

After defeating Rodney with martial arts, the run for the Planes
commenced. Mysterious force was moderately annoying and Rodney
appeared only once in the Mazes of Menace. Planes were quite
unproblematic, even the Plane of Air. The fun really began on the
Astral Plane. I didn't realize that my brave dungeoneer should use his
spare magic lamp to wish for trice corpse and just stone all those
priests and angels. No, instead he put on ring of conflict and free
action (thus removing +5 ring of increase damage). Cutting through
masses of monsters with martial arts was tedious, even with occasional
blast of teleportation or jumping with spell. Facing Pestilence was
easy, but Death was very damaging, shaving some 100 HP before it could
be killed. To make things worse, monk had to visit all three altars to
find the right one.

I was aiming for vegetarian and never-hit-with-wielded-weapon conduct,
but I broke both accidentaly (did not realize tripe is not vegetarian,
then hitting some monster with pick-axe). But in general, I wasn't
eating meat that often and the only weapon I seriously used was silver
saber for shades in Orcus (and few undead along the way).
Unfortunately, martial arts seem to be no match for highly enchanted
artifact weapon, so Monk has quite trouble cutting through monsters
fast. The quick accumulation of intrinsics, on the other hand, is very
nice.

Next role will be lawful human male Priest.

